cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, and also cite
  Sørensen (2013), on which the calculation is based.
title: "Birefringence.jl: computational Michel-Lévy interference colour charts"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Julia package that calculates Michel-Lévy interference colour charts
  from first principles, following Sørensen (2013). Options control the
  light source, white balance and output colour space, and settings are
  included to reproduce the published chart of Sørensen (2013).
authors:
  - given-names: William
    family-names: Davis
version: 0.4.3
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23489857
license: MIT
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23489857"
repository-code: "https://github.com/williamjsdavis/Birefringence.jl"
keywords:
  - birefringence
  - interference colour
  - Michel-Lévy chart
  - optical mineralogy
  - Julia
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - given-names: Bjørn Eske
        family-names: Sørensen
    title: >-
      A revised Michel-Lévy interference colour chart based on
      first-principles calculations
    journal: European Journal of Mineralogy
    year: 2013
    volume: 25
    issue: 1
    start: 5
    end: 10
    doi: 10.1127/0935-1221/2013/0025-2252
